%% ============================================================
%% DIAGRAM 05: PRIVATE-SONG WORKFLOW
%% ============================================================
%% PURPOSE:
%% Combines audio-assisted entry, manual entry, persistence, recommendation use,
%% privacy boundaries, and deletion into one complete private-song lifecycle.
%%
%% EXPLANATION:
%% A listener can upload an audio file for local estimates or enter every music
%% feature manually. Uploaded audio is validated, analyzed, and deleted before a
%% proposal is shown. The listener reviews or corrects the values. Only approved
%% metadata is stored in session-scoped SQLite and added to recommendations. The
%% record remains until the listener deletes it; the audio file never persists.
%%
%% HOW TO READ:
%% Read numbered messages from top to bottom. The first "alt" block shows the two
%% entry methods. Later blocks show review, recommendation use, and deletion.
%%
%% KEY POINT:
%% VYBE stores approved song metadata, not uploaded audio.
%% ============================================================
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Listener
    participant UI as VYBE Interface
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant Audio as Local Audio Analyzer
    participant Model as Local KNN Model
    participant Draft as Temporary Proposal
    participant DB as SQLite Private Catalog
    participant Ranker as Recommender

    Note over Listener,Ranker: Private records are isolated by anonymous session ID

    alt Upload audio for assisted analysis
        Listener->>UI: Select permitted audio and confirm rights
        UI->>API: Upload validated audio
        API->>Audio: Analyze randomized temporary file
        Audio->>Model: Estimate supported genre and mood
        Model-->>Audio: Labels and confidence
        Audio-->>API: Features, estimates, provenance, warnings
        API->>Audio: Delete temporary audio file
        API->>Draft: Store audio-free review proposal
    else Enter all features manually
        Listener->>UI: Enter canonical song values
        UI->>API: Submit validated manual values
        API->>Draft: Store review proposal
    end

    Draft-->>UI: Display editable values and provenance
    alt Listener discards proposal
        UI->>API: Discard
        API->>Draft: Delete proposal
    else Listener approves or corrects proposal
        UI->>API: Submit reviewed metadata
        API->>DB: Save session-owned private song
        API->>Draft: Delete proposal
        DB-->>UI: Private song is available
    end

    opt Listener requests recommendations
        UI->>API: Submit preferences with session cookie
        API->>DB: Load current session's songs
        DB-->>Ranker: Eligible private records
        Ranker-->>UI: Grounded ranked results
    end

    opt Listener deletes the private song
        UI->>API: Delete private song ID
        API->>DB: Delete only within current session
        DB-->>UI: Confirm deletion
    end

    Note over Audio,DB: Temporary audio is deleted. Approved metadata persists until user deletion.
